        "hydrology": "Was permanently water-logged, now seasonally water-logged.",
        "soils": "The soil is a humo-ferric podzol. It is variable across the site, with E and Bh (eluvial and illuvial horizons) not always visible. Where apparent, the E horizon is at 6-17cm depth, with Bh below onto parent material.",
        "vegetation": "Heather makes up >60% of the plant biomass at the site, but Vaccinium myrtillus and Empetrum nigrum are also present. Other plant species present in the experimental plots include:\r\n\r\nVaccinium myrtillus,  Deschampsia flexuosa,*Pleurozium schreberii, *Hypnum jutlandicum, *Psuedosclerum purum, *Plagiothecium undulatum, *Rhytidiadelphus loreus, *Rhytidiadelphus squarrosus, *Hylocomium splendens, *Dicranum scoparium, *Polytrichum formosum. Species with a * indicate bryophytes.\r\n"
      },
